[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5043513372","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121629#issuecomment-5043513372","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121629","id":5043513372,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLJ3oHA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T08:16:39Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T10:31:55Z","body":"Please add performance tests for trivial and nontrivial types.\r\n\r\nMy gut feeling is that the current state is less bad than it looks.\r\nNontrivial types should, normally, have a fast `std::move` path. Which means that the local copy, which needs to be taken anyway, is just made at the caller site instead of the function itself, and then trivially moved in. Rust's entire language bet is on this mechanic, often taking copies instead of references for simplicity, and C++'s move semantics aren't much worse than Rust's in terms of performance.\r\n\r\nEdit: The above is wrong because a) Rust moves destruct, and b) Itanium ABI dictates the caller (instead of callee) destructs, which means the compiler can do less optimization; especially to skip unnecessary copies and the temporary move/dtor.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5043513372/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5044046695","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121629#issuecomment-5044046695","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121629","id":5044046695,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLKYLZw","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T09:15:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T18:41:15Z","body":"### NEW METHOD: \r\nLvalue (Copies) took: 282 ms\r\nRvalue (Moves) took: 78 ms\r\n\r\n### OLD METHOD: \r\nLvalue (Copies) took: 332 ms\r\nRvalue (Moves) took: 119 ms\r\n\r\nBenchmark:\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n\r\nSorry not super neat as my formatting plugin doesn't seem to work with Godot 4...\r\n\r\n```\r\nvoid benchmark_local_vector_push_back() {\r\n\tconst int iterations = 15000000;\r\n\t\r\n\t\r\n\tstruct TestType\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tString sz;\r\n\t\tvoid init(uint32_t n)\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tsz = \"Sample String \" + String::num(n) + \" - This is a heap-allocated string used for benchmarking.\";\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t};\r\n\t\r\n\tLocalVector<TestType> samples;\r\n\tsamples.resize(100);\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\r\n\t\tsamples[i].init(i);\r\n\t}\r\n\t\r\n\tfor (uint32_t loop=0; loop<2; loop++)\r\n\t{\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tLocalVector<TestType> vec;\r\n\t\tvec.reserve(iterations); // Isolates push_back overhead from reallocations\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\tuint64_t start = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_msec();\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\tif (loop == 0)\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tprint_line(\"\\nNEW METHOD: \");\r\n\t\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tvec.push_back(samples[i % 100]);\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\telse\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tprint_line(\"\\nOLD METHOD: \");\r\n\t\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tvec.push_back_old(samples[i % 100]);\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tuint64_t end = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_msec();\r\n\t\tuint64_t elapsed = (end - start);\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\tprint_line(\"Lvalue (Copies) took: \" + itos(elapsed) + \" ms\");\r\n\t}\r\n\t\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tLocalVector<TestType> vec;\r\n\t\tvec.reserve(iterations);\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\tLocalVector<TestType> source_pool;\r\n\t\tsource_pool.reserve(iterations);\r\n\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {\r\n\t\t\tsource_pool.push_back(samples[i % 100]);\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\tuint64_t start = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_msec();\r\n\t\tif (loop == 0)\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tvec.push_back(std::move(source_pool[i]));\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\telse\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {\r\n\t\t\t\tvec.push_back_old(std::move(source_pool[i]));\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tuint64_t end = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_msec();\r\n\t\tuint64_t elapsed = (end - start);\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\tprint_line(\"Rvalue (Moves) took: \" + itos(elapsed) + \" ms\");\r\n\t}\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nThose compile errors I'll have to check out, looks like missing includes in those call sites, might have to work out why it compiled before (maybe it's because of the `PUSH_BACK_BY_VALUE` bool calling in a need for the header, I'll see if I can adjust that).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5044046695/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5044186321","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121629#issuecomment-5044186321","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121629","id":5044186321,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLKgs0Q","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T09:30:30Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T09:30:30Z","body":"Did a quick checkup, and yea, turns out i was totally wrong: Rust moves memcpy and destruct, while c++ still needs the old type to destruct separately. So by taking a copy we're probably paying for the `= nullptr` plus `if (ptr != nullptr)` in move and destruct.\r\nI'll look into what our options are.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5044186321/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5045278461","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121629#issuecomment-5045278461","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121629","id":5045278461,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLLjW_Q","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T11:33:55Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T15:21:41Z","body":"Ideally we'd just switch between them based on `T` (with SFINAE or something), but I suspect it would bring up the compile issue I had earlier where CI fails for some builds because it would depend on the definition of `T` being present, so will have to figure another way around.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5045278461/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5045322081","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121629#issuecomment-5045322081","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121629","id":5045322081,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLLmBYQ","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T11:38:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T11:39:02Z","body":"As said on RC, i'd also be interested in seeing the aliasing-aware version of this as well in comparison, like in `CowData`:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b4fb06cdb3db0c61db40c7b365bfa7adec3cb2ce/core/templates/cowdata.h#L330-L333","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5045322081/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5050145418","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121629#issuecomment-5050145418","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121629","id":5050145418,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLQMaig","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T18:50:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-30T11:54:54Z","body":"> i'd also be interested in seeing the aliasing-aware version of this as well in comparison\r\n\r\nThat's an interesting avenue to pursue - I added it to the benchmark.\r\n\r\nThis particular benchmark:\r\n1) doesn't show a significant slowdown for simple types, although in theory it could be slower (due to the copy being cheaper than the check!)\r\n2) doesn't show a significant benefit for complex types\r\n\r\nThis is likely in part because the benchmark doesn't stress the `grow` branch.\r\n\r\nFor 10,000 complex types, it only takes 14 power of 2 `grows` to get past 10000 elements, so it's only doing 14 temporary copies at most(!), which may be getting drowned out in the benchmark noise.\r\n\r\nTo properly benchmark the address check you would probably need to use small `LocalVectors`, and do it many times, in order to maximise the amount of `grow` branches that are taken, or artificially force a grow on each `push_back`.\r\n\r\nAnyway it's sufficiently different to warrant it's own PR I think.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5050145418/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433266924","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121629#issuecomment-5433266924","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121629","id":5433266924,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ9kS7A","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T01:39:55Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T01:39:55Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433266924/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]